  "observations": [
    "The time-diverse LED and IR pixels consistently show a broad circular upper press platen with a dark used-steel underside; illumination is concentrated at a thin three-wall boundary and contact region rather than a luminous white ceiling.",
    "In the controlled Blender pair, the upper-band luminance mean fell from 0.49409 to 0.42690 and the dark fraction rose from 0.01503 to 0.17840 while the LED boundary remained visible.",
    "In the controlled Unreal pair, the upper-band luminance mean fell from 0.52998 to 0.36515 and the highlight fraction fell from 0.01471 to 0.00059. This removes the largest white-fascia cue but does not fix Unreal's remaining coarse geometry, concrete surface, global lighting and sensor-noise gaps.",
    "The release representatives remain seed-dependent. Their band statistics are evidence that the new bounded range is active, not that either renderer matches the unregistered real ROI.",
    "The real ROI retains camera sharpening, compression, overlay, specular wear and higher-frequency concrete/paint structure that neither procedural scene reproduces."
  ],
